  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Sustainable Development in North Sinai</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Egypt):  This five-year activity seeks to complement the ongoing Government of Egypt (GOE) economic development investments in North Sinai with community-driven development. Economic development in North Sinai lags behind that of other Governorates in Egypt. Development efforts to date have largely focused on large scale infrastructure improvements across the region. However, these large-scale development plans have not always considered local development needs at the grassroots level. This activity will empower local communities by training youth with the skills necessary to develop community initiatives and by improving the economic livelihoods of people living and working in North Sinai with a focus on traditional industries such as fisheries, agriculture and handicrafts. It will also deliver health and education services to under-served Bedouin populations with the objective of advancing the economic and social inclusion of Bedouin communities into the overall fabric of the Egyptian economy. .</narrative>
  </description>
